{"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Suffix-arrays","title":"Suffix arrays","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixArray"]},{"anchor":"Suffix-trees","title":"Suffix trees","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree"]},{"anchor":"Suffix-automata","title":"Suffix automata","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton"]},{"anchor":"Extended-Modules","title":"Extended Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/Trees"],"generated":true}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SuffixStructures"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","title":"SuffixStructures","symbolKind":"module","externalID":"SuffixStructures"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixArray","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" holds the starting positions of a text’s suffixes in sorted order, with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"length of the prefix each shares with the one before it (Manber and Myers, 1990). Every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"occurrence of a pattern is a run of neighbouring suffixes, found by binary search, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"prefix lengths give the longest repeated substring and the number of distinct substrings."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import SuffixStructures","","let banana = SuffixArray(\"banana\")","let found = banana.occurrences(of: \"ana\")","found.map { banana.positions[$0] }   \/\/ [3, 1]","banana.longestRepeatedSubstring      \/\/ 1 ..< 4, \"ana\"","banana.distinctSubstringCount        \/\/ 15"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The text may be any sequence of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Comparable"},{"text":" symbols. For ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UInt8"},{"text":", such as a string’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"utf8"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"construction sorts the bytes themselves in O(","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"text":") (induced sorting: Nong, Zhang and Chan, 2009);","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"any other symbol type is first replaced by its rank among the text’s distinct symbols.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is the compressed trie of the same suffixes, built left to right by Ukkonen’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"algorithm (1995), over one text or several. A pattern is found in O(","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"m"}]},{"text":") steps down from the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"root; the deepest internal node is the longest repeated substring, and the deepest node with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"suffixes of every text below it the longest common substring. Its nodes convert to Grafluent’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"RootedTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":"RootedTree(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and its suffix links are a ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixTree\/suffixLinksView-swift.property","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let both = SuffixTree(texts: [\"xabxac\", \"abcabxabcd\"])","both.longestCommonSubstring?.range.count   \/\/ 4, \"abxa\"","both.occurrences(of: \"ab\").count           \/\/ 4"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton"},{"text":" is the smallest automaton whose paths from its start state spell the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"text’s substrings (Blumer et al., 1985), built one symbol at a time with at most 2","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" − 1","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"states. It answers membership, occurrence counts and first occurrences in O(","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"m"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":") transitions, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"finds the longest substring another text shares by walking that text over it. Its transitions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are a ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/transitionsView-swift.property"},{"text":", and its suffix links convert to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Grafluent’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Arborescence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":"Arborescence(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let automaton = SuffixAutomaton(\"abcbc\")","automaton.occurrenceCount(of: \"bc\")                         \/\/ 2","automaton.longestCommonSubstring(with: \"xbcbz\")?.textRange  \/\/ 1 ..< 4, \"bcb\""]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"in